1️⃣ Difference between spring and springboot
🔹Spring:
Spring is a lightweight java framework that provides:
->dependency injection
->inversion of control
->MVC Architecture
⚠️Drawbacks of using Spring
-> Boilerplate code
-> Too much xml configuration
-> External server
-> Manual Dependency Management

🔹Spring Boot:
Spring boot is built on top of spring for faster development
✅ Advantages:
-> faster development
-> no XML configuration
-> Embedded Server
-> Auto configuration

🔁 comparison table
_________________________________________________________________________
|feature              |   Spring                 |      Springboot      |
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
|configutation        |   xml+java               |      java only       |
|server               |   External               |      Embedded server |
|setup time           |   takes more time        |      less time       |
|Auto configuration   |   not possible           |      possible        |
|Boiler plate         |   more                   |      minimal         |
|_______________________________________________________________________|

📌 Example
Spring (old way)
<bean id="userService" class="com.app.UserService"/>

Spring Boot
@Service
public class UserService {}
👉 No XML, automatic bean creation.
